@BlacklionCTA Not at all. The market is just following his direction. He noted multiple times that the balance sheet is the problem here and what is causing too much accommodation. Market is appropriately reacting to his preference of a reduced Fed footprint in long duration Treasuries.

They want a steeper yield curve. And rightfully so. It's still at record flat levels and continues to create winners and losers in the economy. Steepening the yield curve to natural, untampered with levels is good and important for a healthy economy. It's also a headwind for stocks as we are seeing.

@DerivativesDon @BlacklionCTA Nasdaq is red 6 days in a row. Tech has most to lose from a steeper yield curve while small caps / main street have most to gain. Price action makes complete sense imo.

He can't unilaterally start changing balance sheet policy and we know the committee members don't understand its transmission mechanism and are hardened in their stance to keep current balance sheet policy. That's why he is saying he needs time. To get the committee around to his view on balance sheet. And it's working - that's what the long end is saying.

